{
  "name": "How to Prioritize Repairs in a Rental Property",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Prioritizing repairs in a rental property effectively can save you time, money, and headaches. Here's a smart way to approach it: First, conduct a thorough inspection and document everything, especially any damage or systems that are nearing their end-of-life. Step two is to immediately prioritize anything that impacts tenant safety or habitability. Think plumbing leaks, electrical hazards, or heating issues – these can become urgent and affect occupancy. Next, create a detailed scope of work that outlines exactly what needs to be done. Once you have that, get bids from trusted contractors like HH Remodeling LLC and line up your trades early to avoid delays. The final crucial step is sequencing: always address structural issues and rough-in systems before you even think about cosmetic finishes. Don't get caught up in painting over a problem that needs a deeper fix. For complex repairs involving electrical, plumbing, or structural elements, bringing in a licensed professional is always recommended.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
